<section class="hwaet-projects">
  <h2 class="hwaet-section-title">Projects</h2>

<div class="hwaet-project">
  <h3>Earthburn</h3>
  <p class="hwaet-project-meta">Short Film · In Production</p>
  <p class="hwaet-project-description">
    After two days and nights tending a charcoal burn deep in the forest,
    a medieval Commoner stumbles through a rowdy feast and a delirium of
    prophetic visions before arriving at his fated destination: the
    abandoned corpse of the King of England.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="hwaet-project">
  <h3>Drag Me to Winchester</h3>
  <p class="hwaet-project-meta">Feature Film · In Development</p>
  <p class="hwaet-project-description">
    After finding the fresh corpse of the Norman King of England abandoned
    in the forest, Purkiss, a medieval charcoal burner, must drag the
    miraculously speaking cadaver to Winchester Cathedral, facing ancient
    ghosts, Norman soldiers and even the Devil himself.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="hwaet-project">
  <h3>Finding Folklore</h3>
  <p class="hwaet-project-meta">Podcast &amp; Film Series</p>
  <p class="hwaet-project-description">
    A folk storytelling podcast and online video series exploring the myths
    and legends, fairytales, ghost stories, songs and traditions of England.
    Series One was released in 2024; Series Two is in development.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="hwaet-project">
  <h3>Unannounced HETV Project</h3>
  <p class="hwaet-project-meta">Television Series · In Development</p>
  <p class="hwaet-project-description">
    An eighteenth-century series set in the New Forest, based on the books
    of HWAET founder Brice Stratford.
  </p>
</div>

</section>

  <section class="hwaet-intro">
    <p>HWAET is a creative company founded by James Carney and Brice Stratford.
</p>
<p>
We develop television and film rooted in history and place. Working collaboratively with local communities, historians, craftspeople and cultural organisations, we create productions with distinctive voices and lasting connections to the places from which they emerged.
</p>
